# GSD Core for Cursor

This repo has a project-local GSD Core install for Cursor in `.cursor/`
(skills in `.cursor/skills/gsd-*`, agents in `.cursor/agents/`, workflows in
`.cursor/gsd-core/`). Version: see `.cursor/gsd-core/VERSION`.

- Invoke GSD by mentioning the skill name, e.g. `gsd-resume-work`,
  `gsd-progress`, `gsd-pause-work`, `gsd-execute-phase`.
- The GSD shell snippets look for `gsd-tools.cjs` under `$RUNTIME_DIR` (or the
  repo root), then `.claude/gsd-core`. They do not check `.cursor/gsd-core`, so
  without `RUNTIME_DIR` they would pick up the Claude Code copy in `.claude/`,
  which can be an older version. Before running any GSD workflow shell block,
  run `export RUNTIME_DIR="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/.cursor"` in the
  same shell, or put it at the start of the command.
- `.planning/` is shared with the Claude Code GSD install. Never delete or
  reset it; it holds the paused Phase 2/3 state (`.continue-here.md`).
